=== Call A investigation (2026-07-12T07:xxZ) ===
Live TwitterAPI.io returned 20-50 posts for the list:2067062923525275922 query
(max_pages=1 to 5, max_per_page=5 to 20). Direct API sample shows real
list-member posts by @alexandr_wang (615818451), @RyanLeeMiniMax
(1926868815683497984), and others — Call A is functional.

The "n_posts=0 / nothing to report" output is a smoketest-design quirk:
_load_api_posts filters via detect_brand_mentions(text, compiled_index)
and drops posts whose text has no brand token. Call A's value is WHO said
something, not WHAT they said — for replies/list-member chatter the
author_handle is signal but the text has no brand keyword, so all sampled
posts get dropped before the report.

Concrete: a 5-post smoke run returned 5 posts, all failed detect_brand_mentions
(filtered out), smoketest then short-circuited with "nothing to report"
suppressing the posts_with_no_brand_skipped counter that would explain why.

This is a smoketest UX issue, not a Call A query issue. Workaround for the
operator: use --source=latest-cycle or --source=latest-n to see Call A
posts (those paths don't apply the no-brand filter and surface the full
sample including non-brand-mentioning list-member chatter).
